{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Date Parsing.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Date Parsing.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"date parsing date parsing","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Date Parsing.md","fileName":"Date Parsing.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Date Parsing","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 18:44\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Analytic Data Preparation]] · [[Data Quality and Missing Data]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Analytic Data Preparation","Data Quality and Missing Data","Derived Temporal Feature","analyzinghealthdatainrforsasusers.pdf","essentialsofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Date Parsing.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Date Parsing.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"date parsing date parsing","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Date Parsing.md","fileName":"Date Parsing.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Date Parsing","heading":"Date Parsing","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Date parsing converts a character or factor representation into a date class by specifying the order and format of its components. Month names, numeric months, two- or four-digit years, weekday text, and separators all require matching format codes.\n\nA value that looks like a date on screen may still be text internally. Parsing should therefore be followed by a class check and sample comparison, because a mistaken format can produce missing or misinterpreted dates that contaminate every later time calculation.\n\nIn the book's wrangling pattern, corrected dates become the basis for [[Derived Temporal Feature|derived year and season features]]. Parsing must precede that derivation so apparently valid text does not produce misleading calendar groups.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Analytic Data Preparation","Data Quality and Missing Data","Derived Temporal Feature","analyzinghealthdatainrforsasusers.pdf","essentialsofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Date Parsing.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Date Parsing.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"date parsing date parsing","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Date Parsing.md","fileName":"Date Parsing.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Date Parsing","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[analyzinghealthdatainrforsasusers.pdf]]\n\n[[essentialsofdatascience.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Analytic Data Preparation","Data Quality and Missing Data","Derived Temporal Feature","analyzinghealthdatainrforsasusers.pdf","essentialsofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}